<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guoyu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Discourses of the States</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Guoyu (Discourses of the States) is an ancient Chinese collection of speeches and anecdotes arranged by state, covering Zhou, Lu, Qi, Jin, Zheng, Chu, Wu and Yue from about the tenth to the fifth century BCE. Traditionally attributed to Zuo Qiuming, it was compiled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> and is a major source for the Spring and Autumn period alongside the Zuo zhuan.</p></div>
